   "source": {
    "label": "thm:gre upper bound",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For any tunable parameters $(\\tau_i)_{i = 2}^K \\in \\realset^{K - 1}$, the expected $n$-round regret of \\cref{alg:gre} can be bounded from above as $R(n) \\leq \\sum_{i = 2}^K \\Delta_i (a_i + b_i)$, where $a_i = \\sum_{s = 0}^{n - 1} \\E{\\min \\set{1 / Q_{1, s}(\\tau_i) - 1, n}}$, $b_i = \\sum_{s = 0}^{n - 1} \\prob{Q_{i, s}(\\tau_i) > 1 / n} + 1$."
   },
